From 09745b6c10b79daebfae40753983b3f7a696bb1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: helloydh007 <296340111+helloydh007@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:55:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Python backend: allow selecting the interpreter at runtime

Add an Interpreter setting (URL, defaults to python3) to the Python
backend. When it points to an executable, the session runs the newly
added pure-Python server (src/backends/python/server.py, embedded via
python.qrc) with that interpreter instead of the libpython-linked
cantor_pythonserver binary. Empty or unusable paths fall back to the
embedded server, preserving the previous behaviour.

The external server implements the same wire protocol as the embedded
one (code/model/setFilePath/exit, capture of stdout/stderr, variable
introspection, interrupt handling). Also make the login handshake
tolerate a 'ready' token without a trailing newline and fail cleanly
when the process cannot start.
---
 src/backends/python/python.qrc         |   1 +
 src/backends/python/pythonbackend.cpp  |  12 ++
 src/backends/python/pythonbackend.kcfg |   4 +
 src/backends/python/pythonsession.cpp  |  96 ++++++++-
 src/backends/python/server.py          | 264 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/backends/python/settings.ui        |  39 +++-
 6 files changed, 396 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/backends/python/server.py

